  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe improved approach formulates the optimization problem as a convex program with careful variable transformations to handle non-linear overlaps. It uses CVXPY for structured solution attempts, leveraging efficient identification of maximum overlap conditions. The strategy adapts search dynamics based on progress, balancing exploration and exploitation.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nDefine h \u2208 \u211d^{n_points} with h_i \u2208 [0,1], sum(h_i) = n_points / 2, and for each lag k, sum(h_i (1-h_{i+k})) \u2264 C\u2085 * (n_points / 2). Transform constraints using z variables for h products, ensuring convex relaxations.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na. Initialization:\n   - Use provided initial_h_values as a starting solution\n   - Set up CVXPY variables for h and additional z variables for products\nb. Objective setup:\n   - Minimize C\u2085 subject to overlap constraints\nc. Solving:\n   - Attempt solution with ECOS solver\n   - If infeasible, revert to enhanced Differential Evolution with dynamic parameters\n\n4. Search choices\n- Population size: 150, adaptive mutation (0.2-0.4), CR (0.8-0.95)\n- Dynamic F adjustment based on stagnation (F: 0.7-1.0)\n- Mutation strategy alternates between DE/rand/1 and DE/current-to-rand\n\n5. Compute budget\n- 150 initial solutions, 500 iterations per budget unit\n- Adaptive solver timeouts based on remaining time\n\n6. Validation\n- Strict feasibility checks for h and sum constraints\n- Validate overlap evaluations with actual maximum computation",
